## Solution

**Setup.** Define $f(k) = (-1)^{d(k)}$ where $d(k)$ is the popcount (number of 1-bits) of $k$ in binary, with $f(0)=1$. We seek
$$S = \sum_{k=1}^{2020} f(k)\,k^3 = \sum_{k=0}^{2020} f(k)\,k^3 \quad(\text{since }k=0\text{ contributes }0).$$

**Key tool — block sums.** For $p\ge 0$ let $A_j(p) = \sum_{k=0}^{2^p-1} f(k)\,k^j$. A classical Thue–Morse identity gives
$$A_j(p) = 0 \;\text{ for }\; j < p, \qquad A_p(p) = (-1)^p\, p!\, 2^{p(p-1)/2}.$$
(Verified: $A_1(1)=-1$, $A_2(2)=4$, $A_3(3)=-48$.)

**Carry-free block decomposition.** If $\text{offset}$ is a multiple of $2^p$, then for $0\le k<2^p$ there are no carries, so $f(\text{offset}+k)=f(\text{offset})\,f(k)$, and
$$\sum_{k=0}^{2^p-1} f(\text{offset}+k)(\text{offset}+k)^3 = f(\text{offset})\bigl[\text{offset}^3 A_0(p)+3\,\text{offset}^2 A_1(p)+3\,\text{offset}\,A_2(p)+A_3(p)\bigr].$$

**Binary expansion of 2021.** Since we sum over $[0,2021)$ (i.e. $k=0,\dots,2020$):
$$2021 = 2^{10}+2^9+2^8+2^7+2^6+2^5+2^2+2^0.$$
Process set bits from MSB, maintaining $\text{offset}$ (sum of higher powers already consumed):

| bit $p$ | offset (before) | $f(\text{offset})$ | block contribution |
|---|---|---|---|
| 10 | 0 | $+1$ | $A_0..A_3(10)=0$ (all $j<10$) $\Rightarrow 0$ |
| 9 | 1024 | $-1$ | all $A_j(9)=0$ for $j\le3$ $\Rightarrow 0$ |
| 8 | 1536 | $+1$ | all $A_j(8)=0$ for $j\le3$ $\Rightarrow 0$ |
| 7 | 1792 | $-1$ | all $A_j(7)=0$ for $j\le3$ $\Rightarrow 0$ |
| 6 | 1920 | $+1$ | all $A_j(6)=0$ for $j\le3$ $\Rightarrow 0$ |
| 5 | 1984 | $-1$ | all $A_j(5)=0$ for $j\le3$ $\Rightarrow 0$ |
| 2 | 2016 | $+1$ | see below |
| 0 | 2020 | $-1$ | see below |

For $p\ge 4$, every $A_j(p)=0$ when $j\in\{0,1,2,3\}$, so all those blocks vanish.

**Block $p=2$, offset $=2016$.** Here $A_0(2)=A_1(2)=0$, $A_2(2)=4$, $A_3(2)=18$, and $f(2016)=+1$ (popcount $6$). Thus
$$\text{contrib} = 3\cdot 2016\cdot 4 + 18 = 24192 + 18 = 24210.$$

**Block $p=0$, offset $=2020$.** Only $k=2020$; $A_0(0)=1$, $A_1=A_2=A_3=0$. With $f(2020)=-1$ (popcount $7$):
$$\text{contrib} = -1\cdot 2020^3\cdot 1 = -2020^3.$$

**Total.**
$$S = 24210 - 2020^3.$$

**Reduction mod 2020.** Since $2020^3 \equiv 0 \pmod{2020}$,
$$S \equiv 24210 \pmod{2020}.$$
Compute $24210 = 2020\cdot 12 - 30 = 24240 - 30$, so
$$24210 \equiv -30 \equiv 1990 \pmod{2020}.$$

**Verification of the $p=2$ block directly.** $\;2016^3 - 2017^3 - 2018^3 + 2019^3$. With $a=2016$:
$$a^3-(a+1)^3-(a+2)^3+(a+3)^3 = 12a + 18 = 12\cdot 2016+18 = 24210. \checkmark$$

$$\boxed{S \bmod 2020 = 1990}$$

### PROOF COMPLETE
